{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degrees_two_and_three_exclusive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degrees_two_and_three_exclusive","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L187-L195","doc":"The two degrees are mutually exclusive on one object: an object cannot carry\na volume form of degree `2` **and** one of degree `3`, since each forces its own\nrank.  So a second fundamental object is genuinely a *second object*, not a\nre-reading of the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.altCube_vanishes_at_rank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.altCube_vanishes_at_rank_two","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L182-L185","doc":"And it is absent at rank `2`: `Λ³` of the corpus's fundamental object\nvanishes.  This is why no amount of re-fibring `V` produces the eightfold\nsinglet — see `QOU.Eightfold.FibreFunctorDimensionNotCategorical`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.altCube_dim_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.altCube_dim_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L172-L180","doc":"**The eightfold singlet exists exactly at rank 3.**  The totally\nantisymmetric channel of `W^{⊗3}` — the `𝟏` of `𝟑 ⊗ 𝟑 ⊗ 𝟑 = 𝟏𝟎 ⊕ 𝟖 ⊕ 𝟖 ⊕ 𝟏` — is\none-dimensional iff the rank is `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.complementaryDegree_ne_one_of_three_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.complementaryDegree_ne_one_of_three_le","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L167-L170","doc":"Restated as a non-self-duality statement: for every degree `N ≥ 3` the\ncomplementary power is not `Λ¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degree_three_complementary_is_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degree_three_complementary_is_two","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L160-L165","doc":"**The consequence for the eightfold way.**  At degree `3` the complementary\npower is `Λ²`, not `Λ¹`, so the volume form relates `W` to its *exterior square*\nrather than to itself.  Self-duality is therefore not forced, which is precisely\nwhat `Sym2GateFSTrichotomy.gate_forces_complex_of_dim_three` requires of any\nthree-dimensional object passing the `Sym²` gate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.complementaryDegree_eq_one_iff_degree_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.complementaryDegree_eq_one_iff_degree_two","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L154-L158","doc":"**The dichotomy.**  The complementary degree `N - 1` equals `1` — i.e. the\ndual of `W` is `W` itself, so the volume form makes `W` self-dual — exactly when\nthe degree is `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.complementary_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.complementary_dim","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L145-L152","doc":"**The complementary power has the same dimension as the object.**  For a\nrank-`N` object, `dim Λ^{N-1}W = N = dim W`.  This is the dimension shadow of\n`W^∨ ≅ Λ^{N-1}W`, the isomorphism the volume form induces; the object-level\nstatement is cited, not formalised (see the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degree_three_forces_rank_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degree_three_forces_rank_three","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L141-L143","doc":"The `N = 3` row: a degree-3 volume form forces rank `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degree_two_forces_rank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.degree_two_forces_rank_two","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L136-L139","doc":"The `N = 2` row: the corpus's own volume constraint, recovered.  Matches\n`QOU.BraidsAndKnots.VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.rank_eq_of_volumeForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.rank_eq_of_volumeForm","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L127-L134","doc":"**A volume form forces the rank to be its degree.**  If `Λ^N W ≅ 𝟙` with\n`N ≥ 1`, then `rank W = N`.  The hypothesis `1 ≤ N` is what excludes the\ndegenerate `Λ⁰W ≅ 𝟙`, which holds for every object and says nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.choose_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.choose_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L91-L125","doc":"A binomial coefficient is `1` exactly at the two ends of its row.\n\nThis is the arithmetic core of the whole file: it is what makes \"the volume form\nis an isomorphism onto the unit\" a statement about the *rank*, since `𝟙` is\none-dimensional.  Mathlib has `choose_eq_zero_iff` but no `= 1` companion, so it\nis proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.extPowerDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeFormDegree.extPowerDim","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeFormDegree.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The dimension of `Λ^k W` for an object `W` of rank `n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}